Reason: every event allocated its locals with calloc and freed them on return, and every script call did the same for
its arguments; AM2R makes thousands of these calls a frame, and malloc, free and the heap lock (_malloc_r, _free_r,
KMutexUnlock, __syscall_malloc_lock) came to 2-3% of the CPU time in the profiled rooms (Dolphin perf). Blocks of up
to 32 values now go back to a per-size free list (at most 16 kept per size, about 140 KB at worst) and are reused;
each block records its own size, and a reused block is cleared, so the frame sees the same zeroed memory calloc gave.
Larger blocks still use malloc and free.
Upstream: Speed only, every platform. Retires this patch when merged.

